{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>To inquire of Elohim</b> — four times in the Masorah: here; and the second in Samuel: בלכתו לדרוש אלהים — regarding Saul, when he went to seek the donkeys; and לא יכול דוד ללכת לפניו לדרוש אלהים — in Chronicles, regarding the plague, when he saw the angel striking the people; and ויהי לדרוש אלהים — regarding Uzziah, who inquired of Elohim in battle. Teaches that for all their needs they would come to inquire of Elohim — like that of Saul, who inquired of Elohim regarding his lost property; and like that of David, who prayed concerning the plague; and like that of Uzziah, who prayed concerning his enemies."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:30.667110195Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}